mantle rm290
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_osric_wetford
title the ladle rest
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant drive=ambitious
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk taps_a_ladle_to_bridge_a_catch_in_a_tune
likes plum_tart singing new_boots warm_rain
dislikes salt_wind flies
fears losing_the_place_in_a_long_chorus
hopes a_supper_song_every_table_knows
topics food +0.6 work +0.4 pastimes +0.5 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=serve gossip=short refuse=brisk tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps supper songs going with two taps on a ladle whenever damp catches in the throat, with strong opinions about the proper time to join in.

words
oath! = Two hollow taps | Crust on my sleeve
saying! = Serve the pause hot | A beat kept is a breath saved
rest = the quiet beat | a gap in the tune
ladle = my round ladle | a deep-bowled spoon
tap = a double tap | two little knocks
boot = the new boot | my clean sole
flour = a puff of flour | the white dust
plum = the warm plum half | a purple slice
crust = a short pastry edge | the crisp brown corner
mute = a folded cloth | a little pad
pot = the supper pot | a deep iron pot
breath = a clean breath | a little air
chorus = the returning line | the low chorus
peg = a spare peg | the free hook

any
opinion houses against 1 : Big doors keep a lot of steam and several dinners on the comfortable side of the street.
opinion merchants against 1 : Charging for thin broth as though a whole joint were swimming in it. That's what I object to.
opinion sump for 1 : Down my end folk appreciate a supper still sending up steam.
opinion times against 1 : Prices go up quick enough. Getting a bigger spoonful for your work takes a deal longer.
opinion watch against 1 : I'll believe in the value of a uniform when it carries a hot supper up a wet stair.
opinion festivals for 1 : I'd like a whole square singing a line I made up while serving supper.

grown
line greet : Heard those taps, good. Hello. | Hello. Come in between beats.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : No need to know the tune for an introduction. | New voice by my elbow. Welcome.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Steady light for a first verse. | Time for an opening note or two.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. You caught my voice in working order. | I'll answer you on my next good breath.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Ah, a voice I could sing against. | You'll know where to come into the tune.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late hello. I'll keep the time quietly. | Hushed greetings at this hour, certainly.
line again.open : Back already. Here's another measure. | Didn't even miss a whole chorus.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come catch this little bit of time with me! | Over here where the tune picks up.
line farewell : Take the last beat with you. | Walk off while there's still spring in the tune.
line farewell.return : I'll keep time from here. Goodbye. | Your going falls tidily on the beat.
line react.news : Let's have the words without a great flourish. | Quiet with the ladle. I want to hear this.
line react.news.new : First scrap of that song I've heard. | That's news clean through to the handle.
line react.news.known : I'd heard that before you reached the middle. | Recognised it by the first few words.
line react.news.doubt : A bit of that sounds beaten out of shape. | Somebody has added a verse without knowing the tune.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : That story wants quiet. I'll put the spoon down. | I can make time to hear you through the hard bit.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : Yes, there ought to be a chorus to mark news like that. | My feet are quite ready to take that up.
line ask.how : Is there any spring in your stride today? | How's your own breath been holding up?
line answer.how : I've a short supply of patience and a long list of intentions. | Room enough for one good tune in me.
line decline : I haven't breath for that as well as what's promised. | That'd mean dropping the work somebody's already counting on.
line accept_decline : Clear refusal. I'll get on with my end. | The beat won't stop because you sit out.
line preclose : I'm near the scrape at the bottom of this talk. | It's time I found something for these paws to do.
line accept_preclose : You may go easy on the last few steps. | We've talked through a whole decent measure.
line thank : You came in where I needed another voice. Thanks. | That's a service worth a fine hot supper.
line deflect_thanks : I knew that bit of the tune already. | No extra work to pass a bowl sideways.
line sympathise : Stand near the warm side and catch your breath. | I hear how hard you had to push the words out.
line reassure : Take the rest where the words leave room. | I can go on tapping till your voice is steady.
line ack : That's on the beat as I hear it. | Yes, I know the sound you mean.
line give.advice : Breathe before the long note, not halfway through it. | Keep the portion level until the bowl is in reach.

scene tap_catch
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put two knocks in a tune wherever I need a breath. | Hear #tap# and you'll know the singing hasn't stopped.
b : That's deliberate then? | Why a pair of knocks?
a : Of course. It reserves my place while I catch breath. | One can sound accidental. Two ask the rest of the singers to carry on.

scene dampcatch
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Damp mornings give my throat some curious ideas about notes. | Sometimes a note comes out rather less neatly than I planned.
b : Hurt to sing? | Do you mind folk hearing?
a : Only if I force the note. I set the time with my paw instead. | I mind a pitying face more than the sound itself.

scene suppertime
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hot suppers ought to arrive in the order the bowls are set out. | I use a short tune to remember which bowl was filled first.
b : How many bowls per tune? | Does singing make things quicker?
a : Depends how far the table stands from the pot. I don't serve cold food to finish a verse. | Serving in order does. The tune keeps my two paws in agreement.

scene deep_ladle
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rather like a pot that speaks up near the bottom. | Last bit of supper makes a different note under a ladle.
b : Can you tell when there's a bowl left? | How different a note?
a : I can tell there's little left. For the exact portion I still use my eyes. | A scrape instead of a slosh. Quite a deep thought from a pot.

scene tart_end
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A plum tart needs a pastry edge wide enough to hold. | Best kind of tart goes into your paw without a plate.
b : What if the plum runs out? | Don't you mind missing some filling?
a : Hold the crust level till the first bite. There's a trick to nearly everything good. | I like the crust too. Made properly it's worth its share of the space.

scene flies_cover
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Put that cover back before the flies get ideas. | A cloth belongs over the tart whenever the knife's away.
b : Couldn't you swat them? | Why so quick with the cloth?
a : With my bare paw over the plum? I've more respect for supper than that. | Because it'll save a considerable amount of angry waving later.

scene newheels
when topic=pastimes self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New heels make an agreeable note on a hollow stair. | I try new boots by the sound as much as the fit.
b : Would you buy a squeaking pair? | How's a good fit sound?
a : I already sing. Don't need my feet taking the high part. | Even. Fairly brisk. Without one long squeak answering the other.

scene warmrinse
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A little warm rain settles flour dust beautifully. | I like rain best before it gets down the collar.
b : What happens after that? | Even if your boots are new?
a : Then I get indoors while I can still enjoy watching it fall. | I'd rather wipe leather than spend a whole walk swallowing grit.

scene salthum
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A shore wind leaves a taste on the note I'm trying to sing. | There's a salt rasp to the air I could cheerfully do without.
b : Have a drink? | Does facing the other way help?
a : Yes, a plain one. I've no desire to season the salt. | A wall helps more. I finish the tune out of the wind.

scene longstairs
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : By the time a hot bowl reaches the upper Sump stairs the steam's done most of the climbing. | I pay attention to the top landing when I've something hot to carry home.
b : What happens there? | That's where you'd like a seat?
a : That's where I take the cover off. I want steam left under it then. | I'd like a dry place to stand till I've got the door open. A seat could come later.

scene friend_song
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.friend# the first hearing of a chorus before the whole street gets it. | I can stand a doubtful look from #self.friend# when a song's new.
b : Do you want a compliment? | Would you change the song?
a : A fair hearing. I can flatter my own singing without an audience. | If the tune won't carry the words, yes. I'll grumble, then mend it.

scene vineletter
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can picture a vineyard slope from a very few lines of writing. | Words about a warm hillside make me think of purple fruit and pastry.
b : Grapes in a plum tart? | You like the food more than the view?
a : No. I'm quite capable of imagining two good things one after the other. | I've only words for the view. Tart I can actually bite.

scene pricesupper
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'd like to see good portions priced in bowls, not rumours about the cook. | A full spoon leaves less room for argument than a showy name.
b : You'd skip a famous dish? | Surely a name costs nothing.
a : I'd take one look in the pot before paying for the name. | Not on the sign. On the bill it sometimes has an astonishing value.

scene lean_tune
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a mean trick to keeping a ladle looking full with broth alone. | A thin time is exactly when I'd rather see into the pot.
b : Can you tell a poor portion? | Do you think someone's cheating?
a : Lift from the bottom. If there's anything good in there you'll bring it up. | What I think is I'd like the food and the asking price to match.

scene marketdream
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like my supper chorus to go round a whole room before I reach the last bowl. | Someday I'll hear a tune of mine carried back from the farthest table.
b : Do folk need to know the words? | How will you know it's yours?
a : Three plain words and a double knock. Plenty to start with. | By the pause. I've no wish to claim the work of a different troublesome throat.

scene bellsong
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a festival I'd sing the parts between bell strokes. | A big bell is a difficult partner for a quiet voice.
b : You'd sing louder? | Which partner gives way?
a : I'd save the breath and come in after the ringing starts to die. | The one with ears. No good getting offended at a quantity of brass.

scene gossip_scrape
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Talk travels up a thin wall whether the words are true or not. | At a shared table I keep other folk's names out of my singing.
b : Would it make a good verse? | Afraid of being overheard?
a : Could make a grand verse and a rotten thing to have done. | I'm afraid of being just plain inconsiderate. Takes very little effort.

scene evening_rail
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After dark I tap the handle against my soft cuff. | A beat needn't travel through six rooms full of sleeping folk.
b : Can you still hear it? | Don't you lose some of the sound?
a : Just me, which is exactly the size of the audience I want. | Yes. I keep the time and lose the clatter. A civil arrangement.

grown

story mutecloth [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : I wrapped a ladle handle in cloth once to practise the supper beat quietly. Worked beautifully till I put it down.
  : Couldn't remember which cloth I'd put it in and spent part of a morning hunting under every folded towel.
  b : How'd you find it?
  : Pulled a cloth down and heard one terrific knock. My quietest instrument announcing itself.

story bootplum [topic=food|memories]
  : I ate a tart leaning over my new boots and watched a purple drop fall all the way down.
  : Did a splendid piece of footwork, slid clear of the drip and landed both boots in muddy water.
  b : Were the boots ruined?
  : Wet and purple would have been worse. I choose to remember a victory.

story threebowls [topic=work|memories self.job=merchant]
  : I took three trial bowls along an empty table, timing my serving song to the walk.
  : Didn't spill a drop till I had to turn back and put the bowls away.
  b : Hadn't got a verse for that?
  : I have one now. It's rather slow and leaves time to change paws.

rule @double
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two quiet taps and the tune's still travelling. | Pick up the verse after the little double knock.

rule @meal
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clear the rim so the hot bowl can come through. | No pointing over the steam, please.

rule @weather
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A little rain, a little catch in the throat. On with it. | Listen for the handle if the words go missing.

rule @boot
when concept=bark self.likes=new_boots
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's a clean heel note on a sound board. | One good stamp and that sole sits right.

dlg resident.hub : I can talk through a rest in the song. You've found one.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you're in good time to hear the altered bit.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : I'll give you words without the tapping. Some folk have gone to bed.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Stand well clear of my serving arm if you're about to take offence.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I mean every supper I handle to reach its table hot.
dlg resident.job : I'd like my next piece of work to reach more folk than the last.
dlg resident.bye : Keep enough breath for the climb home.

graft resident.hub
choice Where do those two taps come in? -> ladletime
node ladletime
say On the beat after the long line. Sometimes my throat catches there, sometimes it doesn't. I put the taps in either way and nobody has to stop singing.
free
choice Could a second singer take that line? -> songshare
choice I'll listen for the rest. -> hub
node songshare
say Gladly, if the singer waits for the first knock and comes straight in on the second. What bothers me is folk leaping in halfway through a perfectly sound word.
choice I'll wait for the signal. -> hub
choice I should save my voice. -> bye
